<code>assert !this.empty() => \result == this.get(this.size() - 1);</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that if the stack is not empty, the result of `peek()` is equal to the last item in the stack. Since the stack cannot be empty when `peek()` is called (as it would throw an exception), we don't need to handle the case where the result could be null due to the stack being empty.
